  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "heading",
      "kind": "text",
      "label": "From query command to JSON response",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 60,
      "width": 1180,
      "height": 50,
      "style": "title",
      "decorative": true
    },
    {
      "id": "subheading",
      "kind": "text",
      "label": "Example: reading children of a target. Each continuation starts a new command.",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 110,
      "width": 1180,
      "height": 42,
      "style": "hint",
      "wrap": true,
      "decorative": true
    },
    {
      "id": "invoke",
      "kind": "node",
      "shape": "rect",
      "label": "1. Start a query",
      "detail": "Run query children with the parent target and page limit.",
      "note": "Each invocation creates an interruptible command context. The example asks for children of one target; a later page is a new command carrying the returned cursor.",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170,
      "style": "blue",
      "wrap": true
    },
    {
      "id": "dispatch",
      "kind": "node",
      "shape": "rect",
      "label": "2. Route the command",
      "detail": "Send the request to the structured query handler.",
      "note": "The executable sends query to the structured CLI handler. It does not start the browser server to answer this request.",
      "x": 490,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170,
      "style": "blue",
      "wrap": true
    },
    {
      "id": "open-snapshot",
      "kind": "node",
      "shape": "rect",
      "label": "3. Load Saga state",
      "detail": "Validate inputs, then open the data needed by this query.",
      "note": "For this children query, the CLI validates inputs before opening reviewapp. Product operations also open livingapp using the review session snapshot.",
      "x": 920,
      "y": 170,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170,
      "style": "purple",
      "wrap": true
    },
    {
      "id": "project",
      "kind": "node",
      "shape": "rect",
      "label": "4. Read one page",
      "detail": "The query owner selects records and continuation metadata.",
      "note": "The adapter passes typed inputs such as parent, cursor and limit to the application. The application returns the selected records and continuation metadata.",
      "x": 920,
      "y": 450,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170,
      "style": "green",
      "wrap": true
    },
    {
      "id": "envelope",
      "kind": "node",
      "shape": "rect",
      "label": "5. Encode JSON",
      "detail": "Return schema, ok, snapshot, data and page fields.",
      "note": "The success envelope includes schema, ok, snapshot, data and page. The snapshot identifies the state read; pagination tells the caller whether another request is needed.",
      "x": 490,
      "y": 450,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170,
      "style": "green",
      "wrap": true
    },
    {
      "id": "exit",
      "kind": "node",
      "shape": "rect",
      "label": "6. Finish the command",
      "detail": "Write one response and return the matching exit status.",
      "note": "Ordinary failures are already encoded as JSON. The executable returns their mapped exit status without printing a second error message to stderr.",
      "x": 60,
      "y": 450,
      "width": 300,
      "height": 170,
      "style": "green",
      "wrap": true
    },
    {
